/*Q30. You are developing a Movie Rating System using Java classes, constructors, methods, and the this keyword.
Create a class named Movie with the following instance variables:
• String title — represents the movie title.
• double rating — represents the movie rating.
Constructor
Create a constructor Movie(String title, double rating) that initializes the instance variables using the this keyword.
Methods
Implement the following methods:
• display() — displays the movie title and rating.
• isBlockbuster() — checks whether the movie is a blockbuster based on its rating.
A movie is considered a Blockbuster if its rating is strictly greater than 8.0. Otherwise, it is considered Not a Blockbuster.
The Movie class must implement main() to perform the following operations:
1. Read the movie title and rating.
2. Create a Movie object using the constructor.
3. Call the display() method to display the movie details.
4. Call the isBlockbuster() method to display the movie's blockbuster status.
Input Format:
• The first line contains a string representing the movie title.
• The second line contains a floating-point number representing the movie rating.
Output Format:
• For display(), print the movie details in the format:
Title: <title>
Rating: <rating>
<status>
where <rating> is rounded to one decimal place.
Where <status> is:
• "Blockbuster" — if the rating is greater than 8.0.
• "Not a Blockbuster" — if the rating is less than or equal to 8.0.
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class Movie {
    String title;
    double rating;
 
    Movie(String title, double rating) {
        this.title = title;
        this.rating = rating;
    }
 
    void display() {
        System.out.println("Title: " + title);
        System.out.printf("Rating: %.1f%n", rating);
    }
 
    boolean isBlockbuster() {
        return rating > 8.0;
    }
 
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String title = sc.nextLine().trim();
        double rating = Double.parseDouble(sc.nextLine().trim());
        Movie m = new Movie(title, rating);
        m.display();
        System.out.println(m.isBlockbuster() ? "Blockbuster" : "Not a Blockbuster");
        sc.close();
    }
}
